course: dictionary
lesson: 3057
title: The echidna, an egg-laying mammal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An echidna is a small spiny animal from Australia and New Guinea. It eats ants and termites, catching them with a long sticky tongue. «An echidna is covered in spines that are thick hairs.» So its spines are a kind of hair, not a hard shell.
explain: Scientists call the echidna a mammal, like us, because it has hair and feeds its babies milk. What makes it special is that it lays eggs. «A mother echidna lays one soft egg straight into a pouch.» Most mammals grow their babies inside the mother and are born alive.
explain: The spines help the echidna stay safe. «When frightened it curls into a ball or digs straight down until only its spines show.» It cannot run away quickly, so it uses its spines as a shield instead.
fact: An echidna is a mammal from Australia and New Guinea.
fact: Echidnas are one of only two kinds of mammal that lay eggs. The other is the platypus.
fact: A baby echidna is called a puggle. It hatches from its egg about the size of a jellybean.
fact: Most mammals, such as kangaroos, give birth to live babies. A hedgehog looks a bit like an echidna, but it has live babies.
fact: Echidnas are also called spiny anteaters, because they eat ants.
exercise: «An echidna is covered in spines that are thick hairs.» What are the spines made of? | A hard shell like a turtle | *Thick hairs | Scales like a fish | Feathers
exercise: Which animal lays eggs and still feeds its babies milk? | A dog | A kangaroo | *An echidna | A hedgehog
exercise: What is a baby echidna called? | A cub | A kit | *A puggle | A joey
test: «When frightened it curls into a ball or digs straight down until only its spines show.» What does an echidna do when it is frightened? | Climbs a tall tree | Sings loudly | Runs very fast away | *Curls into a ball or digs down
test: What does an echidna eat, catching it with its long sticky tongue? | *Ants and termites | Leaves and fruit | Fish from rivers | Seeds from the ground
exam: Which of these is true? | Echidnas are born alive, like kangaroos | Echidnas can run faster than dogs | Echidnas live in Antarctica | *Echidnas lay eggs and still feed their babies milk
